From 2f0c7472ecae494005dcf58260a432a6d3c356ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:54:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Tests: inflate's and debug's checks without their exact
 twins (#2924)

inflate_test.c checks inflate_adler32_vector against RFC 1950's definition,
the sums taken modulo at every byte, in place of the byte-at-a-time twin,
and makes its streams' checksums by that definition. debug_test.c's units
test freezes a digest of the vector path's sections, fields and line
addresses over every case, generated while the two paths wrote the same
bytes; debug_test_decode keeps checking each row's meaning. The twin
comparisons stay until the deletion.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EgbxndRcXK2s4tcJhwpfvC
Signed-off-by: David Gonzalez Martin <davidgmbb@gmail.com>
---
 src/buster/compiler/debug_test.c   | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/buster/compiler/inflate_test.c | 39 ++++++++++++++++++------------
 2 files changed, 52 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

