From 25eeda14b2201bd717d6f59bdc440d6fab3fd01c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:59:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Delete inflate's and the DWARF writer's exact twins
 (#2924)

inflate_adler32, the byte-at-a-time twin of inflate_adler32_vector, had no
caller but its test. debug.c's `exact` flag, which wrote every line row
alone instead of four at a time, leaves debug_line, debug_sections,
debug_prepare, debug_write and DebugPlan; the rows the groups stop before
are still written one at a time. c_check_debug.c's call drops the argument
(its own exact path stays). benchmark-debug times the one writer, without
--only and --after-scalar.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EgbxndRcXK2s4tcJhwpfvC
Signed-off-by: David Gonzalez Martin <davidgmbb@gmail.com>
